# Nmap Strategy (SpiderFeet CLI Profiling)

**Skill (commands/parser):** `.cursor/skills/nmap/SKILL.md`  
**Formal plan:** `.docs/docs-for-cli-tools/examination_plans/nmap_formal_examination_plan.md`  
**Exploration evidence:** `.docs/docs-for-cli-tools/examination_plans/nmap_exploration_report.md`

## Runtime on this project

| Environment | Scan type | Notes |
|-------------|-----------|-------|
| Windows (default) | `-sT` TCP connect | Works without admin; use for harvest manifest |
| Windows + admin / Linux / WSL | `-sS` SYN | Faster; preferred for production module when privileged |
| Windows | `-O` alone | Often **no** `osmatch` in XML on connect scans |
| Windows | `-A` | Reliable OS + version + NSE bundle for permissive targets |

Always capture **XML to stdout** (`-oX -`) for structured parsing; run a **paired text run** without `-oX` for the Text tab.

## Target classes

| Class | Target | Purpose |
|-------|--------|---------|
| Permissive | `scanme.nmap.org` | Maximum semantic breadth (open/filtered TCP, UDP, versions, OS, NSE, traceroute) |
| Corporate | `bbc.co.uk` | Filtered-heavy ports; sparse open set |
| Local L2 | `192.168.1.0/24`, enrich `192.168.1.12` | Multi-host discovery; Windows SMB/RPC/http-alt |

## Phase order (do not skip)

1. **Host discovery** — `-sn` on single host and CIDR before port scans.
2. **TCP port scan** — `--top-ports` with `--open` on permissive; note `filtered` on corporate.
3. **Service version** — `-sV` on known open ports from step 2.
4. **OS fingerprint** — `-A` on open ports (not standalone `-O` on Windows connect scans).
5. **NSE** — `-sC` on web/SSH ports for script tables distinct from `-sV`.
6. **UDP** — `-sU --top-ports N` for `open`, `closed`, `open|filtered` semantics.
7. **Traceroute** — `--traceroute` on one open port for hop chain.
8. **Skip ping** — `-Pn` when discovery would miss a host behind no-ICMP firewall.
9. **Capstone** — `-A --top-ports 1000 --open` all-in-one on permissive target.

## Semantic archetypes → nugget focus

| Archetype | Command signature | Primary nuggets |
|-----------|-------------------|-----------------|
| A | `-sn` | Scan head, `IP_ADDRESS`, hostname, host up/down |
| B | `-sn <cidr>` | Multiple hosts; scan `contains` each live IP |
| C | `-sT --top-ports --open` | `TCP_PORT_OPEN`, service name |
| D | corporate top ports | Mostly filtered (descriptor, not open port) |
| E | `-sV` | `SOFTWARE_USED`, product/version/CPE |
| F | `-A` | `OPERATING_SYSTEM` (`osmatch`), versions, NSE |
| G | `-sC` | `script` output → banners, keys, titles |
| H | `-sU` | `UDP_PORT_OPEN`; policy for `open\|filtered` |
| I | `--traceroute` | Trace hops → IP + hostname chain |
| J | `-Pn` | Host up without ICMP discovery phase |
| K | capstone `-A` | Combined E+F+G on many ports |
| L | local `-A` | Windows SMB scripts, Service Info OS |

Use only ontology relations: `contains`, `has`, `listens on`. Scan head `contains` discoveries.

## When to escalate

| Observation | Next command |
|-------------|--------------|
| 0 hosts from `-sn` | `-Pn` then TCP ping ports `-PS80,443 -sn` |
| All ports filtered | Corporate target or `-sT -T2`; document filtered semantics |
| No `osmatch` after `-O` | Retry with `-A` or NSE `smb-os-discovery` on 445 |
| `open\|filtered` UDP | Do not emit `UDP_PORT_OPEN` without policy; record ambiguity |

## Harvest

```bash
python .seed/scripts/cli_corpus/harvest.py --tool nmap --dry-run
python .seed/scripts/cli_corpus/harvest.py --tool nmap
```

Evidence: `.docs/docs-for-cli-tools/app_examination_docs/nmap/<n>_*.`

## Deferred (out of initial corpus)

SYN-only (`-sS`), IPv6-only, full `-p-`, `vuln` NSE, idle scan, ARP `-PR` separate from `-sn` on LAN.
